CREATED:20260304T155718Z
DESCRIPTION:Electrophilic Deauration of Gold(I) α-Styrenyl Complexes with 
 Carbon and Silicon Electrophiles\n\nElectrophilic deauration of gold(I) a
 lkenyl complexes involving electrophilic attack of the Ca=Cb p-bond with 
 delivery of the electrophile to Cb is not well understood and direct expe
 rimental evidence is lacking. For this reason\, we sought out bulky silyl
 ium and triarylcarbenium ions that would bias toward electrophilic b-deau
 ration in gold(I) alkenyl complexes and probe said mechanism.\n\nWe found
  reaction of the styrenyl complex (P)AuC(Ph)=CH2 [P = P(t-Bu)2o-biphenyl\
 ; 1a] in CD2Cl2 at -80 °C with [Ph3C][B(C6F5)4] forms a 3.4:1:3.9 mixture
  of the b-electrophilic deauration product\, (E)-1\,3\,3\,3-tetraphenylpr
 opene\, styrene\, and the cationic bis(gold) complex (3a). Reaction of 1a
  with [(4-C6H4OMe)3C][B(C6F5)4] (5)\, in an equimolar mixture in CD2Cl2 a
 t 25 °C\, forms a 3.3:1:4.9 mixture of (E)-1-phenyl-3\,3\,3-trisanisylpro
 pene (6a)\, styrene\, and the cationic bis(gold) complex (3a)\, which fol
 lowed first-order kinetics to ~3 half-lives. A plot of log(k'X/k'H)\, whe
 re k' is the rate of b-alkylation\, plotted versus the Hammett s constant
  displayed a great fit with R2 > 0.99 and a large negative reaction const
 ant (r = -3.44).\n\nThis large negative reaction constant indicates the r
 ate of the electrophilic deauration of para-substituted a-styrenyl gold c
 ompounds is strongly dependent and highly sensitive to the electron-donat
 ing ability of the aryl groups and is consistent with a significant loss 
 of electron density at Ca in the transition state of b-electrophilic deau
 ration. Though this is the case\, the superior fit to the Hammett s const
 ant and apparent zero-order rate constant of 5\, make the intimate detail
 s of the mechanism somewhat unclear.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260304T155718Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260318T143000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260304T155718Z
