DESCRIPTION:<b>REGISTRATION</b>: <a href="https://forms.office.com/Pages/R
 esponsePage.aspx?id=TsVyyzFKnk2xSh6jbfrJTI9QJhcY12JAolV5CeByrWpUOThLR0hQR
 0tQMkZLQ0NTVDFHUExHSlNKSy4u" target="_blank">Click Here</a>\n\n<i>NOTE: P
 lease register ahead of the event.</i>\n\nJoin us for the Duke Office of 
 Scientific Integrity's Research Town Hall "From Design to Dissemination: 
 Working with Research Data at Duke" on March 18th from 3:30 - 5:00pm. \n\
 nResponsible data management\, stewardship\, and sharing are foundational
  to the conduct of high quality research. Our expert panel of speakers wi
 ll share effective strategies to help you manage and steward data\, revie
 w principles of open scholarship and data sharing\, and highlight resourc
 es to support research teams at Duke. \n\nAttending this event fulfills t
 he <b>RCR-200</b> requirement for Faculty and Staff and the <b>714</b> RC
 R credit for graduate students. Participants must attend for at least 60 
 minutes to receive credit.
DURATION:PT1H30M
